ac670b17-5a8b-4f32-91f5-a171a86a6b7e	801f5e53-66b0-4153-875e-11e695ec6a03	c078d4f8-a147-437d-9500-532821147782	2	assistant	agent	screen_analyzer	\N	**Problem:** LeetCode "Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters" (Medium). Given a string `s`, return the length of the longest substring with no repeated characters. The starter code is Python3: `def lengthOfLongestSubstring(self, s: str) -> int`.\n\n**Solution (sliding window with a last-seen index map):**\n\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def lengthOfLongestSubstring(self, s: str) -> int:\n        last = {}          # char -> most recent index\n        left = 0           # start of current window\n        best = 0\n        for right, ch in enumerate(s):\n            if ch in last and last[ch] >= left:\n                left = last[ch] + 1   # jump past the previous occurrence\n            last[ch] = right\n            best = max(best, right - left + 1)\n        return best\n```\n\n**Approach:**\n- Keep a window `[left, right]` that never contains duplicates.\n- When `s[right]` already appears inside the window, move `left` to one past that character's previous index.\n- Update the character's latest index, then record the window length if it is the largest so far.\n\n**Complexity:**\n- Time: O(n), a single pass with O(1) dictionary operations.\n- Space: O(min(n, m)), where m is the alphabet size.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `"abcabcbb"` → 3\n- `"bbbbb"` → 1\n- `"pwwkew"` → 3\n- `""` → 0	claude-sonnet-5-5	1008	470	4634	{}	2026-09-30 05:05:08.746438+00	2026-09-30 05:05:08.718398+00
