cf90b6f3-9abf-4578-b4b0-5af4703167bc	534c4b25-c5a4-4cec-9e2c-f9423b4e711f	1a0ae2d4-34d1-4461-b9bd-1d1c18c516e0	2	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	**Question: What is the difference between Django and Flask?**\n\n**Suggested answer:**\n\nDjango and Flask are both Python web frameworks, but they take very different approaches. Flask is a lightweight, minimalist framework—it gives you the essentials to build a web app and lets you choose your own tools for everything else. Django, on the other hand, is a full-featured, batteries-included framework that comes with built-in solutions for databases, authentication, admin panels, and ORM out of the box.\n\nThe trade-off is flexibility versus convention. Flask is great if you want fine-grained control and are building something custom or small-scale. Django is better when you want to move fast on a larger project and benefit from established patterns and built-in security features. I'd choose Flask for a microservice or API, but Django for a full-featured web application where the built-in tooling saves time.	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	667	210	3077	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "unknown"}}	2026-09-30 05:42:56.46124+00	2026-09-30 05:42:57.080832+00
