b89be802-b330-4f88-ba6d-787e8f2d8882	0adb9676-1aa8-4d56-a6d2-b893cccdebf1	8d76c202-059b-4c3c-8ea0-fcba5a03f13c	4	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	**Question: What is the difference between Django and FastAPI?**\n\nDjango and FastAPI solve different problems. Django is a full-featured, batteries-included framework—it gives you the ORM, admin panel, templating, authentication, all built in. It's great for traditional web applications where you need a lot of scaffolding. FastAPI, on the other hand, is a lightweight, modern framework focused on building APIs quickly. It's faster to start with and gives you automatic API documentation, built-in validation using Python type hints, and excellent async support out of the box. So if you're building a monolithic web app with server-side rendering, Django is your choice. If you're building a REST API or microservice, or you need high performance with async operations, FastAPI is often better. The trade-off is that with FastAPI you build more yourself, whereas Django handles more for you. I'd choose based on what the project actually needs.	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	858	218	3620	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "unknown"}}	2026-09-30 05:52:16.501524+00	2026-09-30 05:52:16.117641+00
