ecc9338f-60a5-4f42-ada4-a7a12e90b412	6ca0434d-e90c-49b5-833e-5687b4262a70	36a2a0df-0fd5-4019-9425-ab039b17b506	2	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	**Question: Compare FastAPI, Flask, and Django.**\n\nHere's a strong answer:\n\n"FastAPI and Flask are both lightweight frameworks, but FastAPI is built on modern async capabilities and automatically generates interactive API documentation—it's really optimized for building APIs quickly. Flask is more minimal and flexible; you have more control but write more boilerplate yourself.\n\nDjango is in a different category—it's a full-featured framework with built-in ORM, authentication, admin panel, and database migrations. It's heavier but gives you a lot out of the box, which is great for larger applications where you need those features fast.\n\nSo the choice depends on your use case: FastAPI if you're building a modern API, Flask if you want simplicity and flexibility, and Django if you need a complete web framework with database and admin tooling already included."	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	671	197	3041	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "unknown"}}	2026-09-30 05:55:54.619965+00	2026-09-30 05:55:54.964296+00
