c843b175-4175-479c-b303-e1ab20343fe1	6ca0434d-e90c-49b5-833e-5687b4262a70	2bf98e84-f168-4105-b9cc-747d3bcfc68b	57	assistant	agent	screen_analyzer	\N	**Problem:** LeetCode 4, *Median of Two Sorted Arrays*. Given sorted arrays `nums1` (size m) and `nums2` (size n), return the median of the combined sorted array in **O(log(m+n))** time.\n\n**Solution (binary search on the partition of the shorter array), Python:**\n\n```python\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass Solution:\n    def findMedianSortedArrays(self, nums1: List[int], nums2: List[int]) -> float:\n        # Always binary search the shorter array\n        if len(nums1) > len(nums2):\n            nums1, nums2 = nums2, nums1\n\n        m, n = len(nums1), len(nums2)\n        half = (m + n + 1) // 2\n        lo, hi = 0, m\n\n        while lo <= hi:\n            i = (lo + hi) // 2       # elements taken from nums1 into left half\n            j = half - i             # elements taken from nums2 into left half\n\n            l1 = nums1[i - 1] if i > 0 else float('-inf')\n            r1 = nums1[i]     if i < m else float('inf')\n            l2 = nums2[j - 1] if j > 0 else float('-inf')\n            r2 = nums2[j]     if j < n else float('inf')\n\n            if l1 <= r2 and l2 <= r1:\n                # Correct partition found\n                if (m + n) % 2 == 1:\n                    return float(max(l1, l2))\n                return (max(l1, l2) + min(r1, r2)) / 2.0\n            elif l1 > r2:\n                hi = i - 1           # took too many from nums1\n            else:\n                lo = i + 1           # took too few from nums1\n```\n\n**Approach:**\n- Split both arrays so that the left parts together contain `(m+n+1)//2` elements, and every element on the left is ≤ every element on the right.\n- Binary search on `i`, the cut position in the shorter array. The cut in the longer array is `j = half - i`.\n- A partition is valid when `nums1[i-1] <= nums2[j]` and `nums2[j-1] <= nums1[i]`.\n- If the total length is odd, the median is `max(l1, l2)`. If even, it is `(max(l1, l2) + min(r1, r2)) / 2`.\n- Sentinels of ±∞ handle empty sides.\n\n**Complexity:**\n- Time: O(log(min(m, n))), which satisfies the O(log(m+n)) requirement.\n- Space: O(1).\n\n**Checks:**\n- `[1,3]`, `[2]` → 2.0\n- `[1,2]`, `[3,4]` → 2.5\n\n**Note:** The OCR'd signature reads `nums1: List[int]`. Make sure `List` is imported, or use `list[int]` as in the second parameter, if you're not using LeetCode's default prelude.	claude-sonnet-5-5	1044	937	7783	{}	2026-09-30 06:00:45.084803+00	2026-09-30 06:00:44.757731+00
