37409339-93d4-4179-87d7-ed08f8981548	45b2c36d-1a8e-497d-9281-352e190107df	e8df59ca-1991-4f39-a6f4-a3014d8b4696	1114	assistant	agent	screen_analyzer	\N	**Problem:** Return the longest common prefix of an array of strings, or "" if none (1 ≤ n ≤ 200, length ≤ 200).\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\n1. Take the first string as the initial prefix\n2. For each other string s:\n3.   While s does not start with prefix: drop the last char of prefix\n4.   If prefix is empty, return ""\n5. Return prefix\n```\n\n**Code:**\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def longestCommonPrefix(self, strs: list[str]) -> str:\n        prefix = strs[0]\n        for s in strs[1:]:\n            # Shrink prefix until s starts with it\n            while not s.startswith(prefix):\n                prefix = prefix[:-1]\n                if not prefix:\n                    return ""\n        return prefix\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- Idea: The common prefix can only shrink as each string is compared.\n- Why correct: After string i, prefix is common to strings 0..i.\n- Edge cases: single string, empty string, no common prefix, identical strings, all handled.\n- Complexity: O(S) time (S = total chars), O(1) space; brute force over all prefixes costs more.\n\n**Alternate method:** Vertical scan by column, O(S) time/O(1) space; stops at the first mismatch, so it is faster when the prefix is short.	claude-sonnet-5-5	5415	443	4308	{}	2026-10-02 03:38:53.904389+00	2026-10-02 03:38:54.083638+00
