a0deabc8-c52e-4551-ae7b-4863c9f0f790	99f867b6-5a3f-47f3-b36d-0953ece54fe7	2a4fb116-4536-4cb5-8fcb-f8a2d2a7c41b	107	assistant	agent	screen_analyzer	\N	**Problem:** Implement `retrieve(question, top_k)` and `query(question)` for the RAG class, using the provided helpers. The OCR cuts off the exact signatures and the expected `query` output, so I assumed `top_k=3` and that `query` returns the retrieved text as a string.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\n1. retrieve: if no documents, return []\n2. embed question with _embed (current vocab)\n3. score each stored embedding with _cosine_similarity\n4. sort indices by score descending, keep top_k with score > 0\n5. query: call retrieve; if empty, return a fallback message\n6. else join retrieved docs into a context string and return it\n```\n\n**Code:**\n```python\nfrom typing import List\nimport numpy as np\nimport re\n\nclass RAGApplication:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.documents: List[str] = []\n        self.embeddings: List[np.ndarray] = []\n        self.vocab = {}\n\n    # ---- provided helpers (unchanged) ----\n    def _tokenize(self, text: str) -> List[str]:\n        return re.findall(r"\\w+", text.lower())\n\n    def _build_vocab(self, texts: List[str]):\n        words = set()\n        for t in texts:\n            words.update(self._tokenize(t))\n        self.vocab = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(sorted(words))}\n\n    def _embed(self, text: str) -> np.ndarray:\n        v = np.zeros(len(self.vocab))\n        for tok in self._tokenize(text):\n            if tok in self.vocab:\n                v[self.vocab[tok]] += 1\n        return v\n\n    def _cosine_similarity(self, a, b) -> float:\n        d = np.linalg.norm(a) * np.linalg.norm(b)\n        return float(a @ b / d) if d else 0.0\n\n    def add_documents(self, documents: List[str]):\n        self.documents.extend(documents)\n        self._build_vocab(self.documents)\n        self.embeddings = [self._embed(d) for d in self.documents]\n\n    # ---- to implement ----\n    def retrieve(self, question: str, top_k: int = 3) -> List[str]:\n        if not self.documents or top_k <= 0:\n            return []\n        q = self._embed(question)\n        scores = [self._cosine_similarity(q, e) for e in self.embeddings]\n        order = sorted(range(len(scores)), key=lambda i: scores[i], reverse=True)\n        return [self.documents[i] for i in order[:top_k] if scores[i] > 0]\n\n    def query(self, question: str, top_k: int = 3) -> str:\n        docs = self.retrieve(question, top_k)\n        if not docs:\n            return "No relevant information found."\n        return "Based on the documents: " + " ".join(docs)\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- Idea: embed the question in the same vocabulary, then rank documents by cosine similarity.\n- Why correct: the query and documents share one vocab, so vector dimensions align.\n- Edge cases: no documents, zero-norm vector, no word overlap, top_k larger than the document count, ties (all handled).\n- Complexity: O(N·V + N log N) time, O(N·V) space; brute force over raw text would be slower.\n\n**Alternate method:** `heapq.nlargest` or `np.argsort` for top-k is O(N log k) and saves a little time. TF-IDF weighting gives better relevance but costs extra code.	claude-sonnet-5-5	5984	1486	9913	{}	2026-10-15 05:43:21.489366+00	2026-10-15 05:43:21.607492+00
