7d9221ef-5cf1-4294-8ca2-436dd6c9eba8	02df8b6e-6dee-4f4e-90fd-12cd3c469fab	12907157-cf2a-4e18-a7a4-f95dade24c04	2	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Difference between Deployment, StatefulSet and DaemonSet in Kubernetes\n**Deployment = stateless interchangeable replicas; StatefulSet = stable identity and storage per pod; DaemonSet = one pod per node.**\n- Deployment: ReplicaSet-managed, rolling updates and rollback, random pod names. Fits APIs (FastAPI/Gin services on EKS).\n- StatefulSet: stable names (pod-0, pod-1), headless Service DNS, per-pod PVC via `volumeClaimTemplates`.\n- StatefulSet: ordered start/stop and updates. Fits Kafka, Postgres, Redis clusters. I used managed RDS/MSK instead.\n- DaemonSet: one pod on every node, or a subset via nodeSelector/tolerations. Fits log shippers (Fluent Bit), node-exporter, CNI.\n- Rule: stateless gets Deployment, needs identity or disk gets StatefulSet, node-level agent gets DaemonSet.	claude-sonnet-5-5	7034	853	7089	{"roles": {"interviewee": "unknown", "interviewer": "unknown"}}	2026-10-21 06:57:05.830289+00	2026-10-21 06:57:05.910224+00
