09e4243c-582e-42f8-828f-be66069c0cc0	02df8b6e-6dee-4f4e-90fd-12cd3c469fab	de1f6a74-7575-4d57-8b07-d05e8627fc30	26	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Kubernetes resource requests vs limits\n**Requests = guaranteed minimum the scheduler uses for placement; limits = hard ceiling enforced at runtime.**\n- Scheduler places pods by the sum of requests per node, not by actual usage.\n- CPU over limit is throttled (CFS quota). Memory over limit is OOMKilled.\n- QoS classes: Guaranteed (requests=limits), Burstable, BestEffort. BestEffort pods are evicted first under node pressure.\n- HPA CPU utilization % is measured against requests.\n- Practice: memory request=limit; CPU limit loose or omitted to avoid throttling. Enforce defaults with LimitRange/ResourceQuota.	claude-sonnet-5-5	7859	604	5115	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "unknown"}}	2026-10-21 06:59:20.367902+00	2026-10-21 06:59:20.591517+00
