2a061a91-e1ff-47be-94b7-ff54e2a2aef8	02df8b6e-6dee-4f4e-90fd-12cd3c469fab	e84bdb0e-9912-42da-b26a-e024f365da24	41	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: What do you mean by "limits are a hard ceiling, enforced"?\n**The kubelet and container runtime enforce the limit via cgroups. CPU over the limit is throttled; memory over the limit is OOMKilled.**\n- CPU is compressible: the CFS quota pauses the container, so latency rises but the pod survives.\n- Memory is incompressible: exceeding the limit gets the container OOMKilled (exit 137), then restarted per `restartPolicy`.\n- Requests only guarantee the minimum and drive scheduling. Limits cap actual usage.\n- Example: a LangChain/RAG service loading embeddings hits its memory limit and is OOMKilled, so set the memory limit with headroom.\n- Debug with `kubectl describe pod` (Reason: OOMKilled) and the Prometheus metric `container_cpu_cfs_throttled_periods_total`.	claude-sonnet-5-5	8271	582	5081	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-21 07:00:28.521834+00	2026-10-21 07:00:28.716838+00
