79454cbe-6ad3-4345-94ca-033932401a2f	02df8b6e-6dee-4f4e-90fd-12cd3c469fab	e8c33c4e-e8cc-4f65-af7d-9dc66b856c56	48	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Kubernetes liveness vs readiness (and startup) probes\n**Liveness = restart the container if it is stuck; readiness = remove the pod from Service endpoints without restarting; startup = holds the other probes off until the app has booted.**\n- Liveness failure: kubelet kills the container and restarts it per `restartPolicy`. Use it for deadlocks or hung processes.\n- Readiness failure: pod is pulled from Service endpoints and gets no traffic, but keeps running. Use it for warm-up, or when a dependency such as DB, Redis or Kafka is down.\n- Startup probe: liveness and readiness are disabled until it succeeds. Protects slow starters, e.g. loading embedding models, from restart loops.\n- Pitfall: don't check downstream dependencies in liveness, or an outage causes cascading restarts. Keep it a cheap `/healthz`.\n- Readiness also gates rolling updates: new pods must be Ready before old ones terminate.	claude-sonnet-5-5	8629	352	7762	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-21 07:02:23.283931+00	2026-10-21 07:02:22.976121+00
