343c9419-83ad-44f1-b374-010d5d49517a	02df8b6e-6dee-4f4e-90fd-12cd3c469fab	388c9f95-9e02-4214-9e5b-5286b7291840	62	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Kubernetes autoscaling: what it is and how it's done\n**Autoscaling adjusts capacity to load automatically: HPA scales pod count, VPA resizes pod requests, Cluster Autoscaler/Karpenter scales nodes.**\n- HPA: compares metric to target (e.g. 70% CPU of requests); `desired = ceil(current × current/target)`.\n- Needs metrics-server and CPU/memory `requests` set; custom metrics via Prometheus Adapter or KEDA.\n- KEDA: scale on Kafka consumer lag or queue depth, including to zero. Fits event-driven consumers.\n- Cluster Autoscaler/Karpenter: adds nodes when pods are Pending for lack of resources; removes underused nodes.\n- Tune `minReplicas`/`maxReplicas`, stabilization window to avoid flapping. VPA and HPA shouldn't both act on CPU.	claude-sonnet-5-5	9203	339	3334	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-21 07:03:59.891981+00	2026-10-21 07:03:59.721516+00
