1e4f1642-7eff-4af3-aeb1-dd882bb1cced	dd95af7c-f247-464d-9525-e7586117b032	df92604f-7ce4-4889-841e-41cb9b57e240	101	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Agent workflow structure (parallel or sequential?), and whether you've used LangGraph or other agent frameworks\n**Sequential per notice with a bounded critique loop; parallel across notices; built as a LangGraph state graph.**\n\n- Per notice: Summarizer → Reply → Critic. Each stage depends on the previous output, so no intra-notice parallelism.\n- Critic loop: conditional edge back to Reply until approved or [N] max iterations, then human review.\n- Parallelism: SQS fan-out, one message per client/notice, Lambda workers scale concurrently.\n- Supervisor agent routes between agents and holds shared state (notice data, drafts, critique).\n- LangGraph: nodes = agents, conditional edges = critique loop, state persisted for resume.\n- Fallbacks: API automation first, then web automation, then OCR-based RPA.	claude-sonnet-5-5	10117	838	7964	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-21 11:09:56.768132+00	2026-10-21 11:34:13.010645+00
