2d57b645-e85a-42dd-80af-385cc4780589	dd95af7c-f247-464d-9525-e7586117b032	451f6183-afad-40ce-bba6-7e584082a021	104	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: LangGraph only, right? Then "What is Redis…" (cut off, most likely what Redis is and how you used it)\n**Redis is an in-memory key-value store; used here as a cache in front of the DB, plus queues and streams elsewhere.**\n\n- LangGraph: confirm yes, plus LangChain for the RAG pipelines.\n- Audit platform: Redis caching for KPIs, job tracker and rules/template lookups, fewer DB reads.\n- Read-replica DB plus Redis keeps API reads fast; the heavy work stays async on SQS/Lambda.\n- Other projects: Redis Streams for real-time chat, Celery broker, sessions.\n- Trade-offs: TTL/invalidation for staleness; cache-aside pattern.	claude-sonnet-5-5	10352	579	5237	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-21 11:10:02.00602+00	2026-10-21 11:34:13.044396+00
c8b2b77b-40b8-4f75-9e36-1cc3225d6408	dd95af7c-f247-464d-9525-e7586117b032	677bf0d2-590b-4023-8e23-a3e17ff2b7bf	105	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: What is a reducer in LangGraph?\n**A reducer is a function on a state key that defines how a node's update is merged into existing state, instead of overwriting it.**\n\n- Declared via `Annotated[list, operator.add]`; the built-in `add_messages` reducer appends and dedupes chat messages by ID.\n- Default without a reducer: the last write overwrites the key.\n- Parallel nodes writing the same key need a reducer, otherwise LangGraph raises `InvalidUpdateError`.\n- Signature: `(current_value, update) -> new_value`. Custom reducers can merge dicts or keep the latest N items.\n- Audit use: accumulate critic feedback and draft revisions across the critique loop [if state held a history list].	claude-sonnet-5-5	10323	512	4635	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-21 11:10:06.641536+00	2026-10-21 11:34:13.055113+00
