1534a75f-e07a-49b8-b9b6-dd51e9644bd7	dd95af7c-f247-464d-9525-e7586117b032	a545c6a6-1f84-4036-bcd4-b41b6342729e	107	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: What is a reducer in LangGraph?\n**A reducer is a function on a state key that defines how each node's update is merged into existing state, instead of overwriting it.**\n\n- Signature: `(current, update) -> new`. Declared as `Annotated[list, operator.add]` in the state schema.\n- Default with no reducer: last write overwrites the key.\n- Parallel nodes writing the same key in one step need a reducer, otherwise `InvalidUpdateError`.\n- Built-in `add_messages` appends messages and replaces existing ones with the same ID.\n- Audit use: accumulate critic feedback and draft revisions across loop iterations [if state held a history list].	claude-sonnet-5-5	10290	506	4936	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-21 11:10:12.930131+00	2026-10-21 11:34:13.080175+00
