60f201d0-5e55-42ab-872d-5c364fe4aecb	e71a240b-ca75-48ea-ac92-1b6e986e0621	3a9d5fd3-f494-47e3-afb8-d094f84b9c75	72	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Core logic: extract sensitive data from text already in a variable\n**Run regex detectors, validate with checksum, return findings (type, span, page) without raw values.**\n- Aadhaar: `\\b\\d{4}\\s?\\d{4}\\s?\\d{4}\\b`, then Verhoeff checksum to cut false positives\n- PAN `\\b[A-Z]{5}\\d{4}[A-Z]\\b`; mobile `(?<!\\d)(?:\\+91[\\s-]?)?[6-9]\\d{9}(?!\\d)`\n- Loop `re.finditer` per pattern, keep `m.start()`/`m.end()`, store `{type, page, start, end, confidence}`\n- Names: NER (Presidio or Comprehend `DetectPiiEntities`), since regex can't find names\n- Mask: `text[:s] + "X"*(e-s) + text[e:]`, applied right-to-left so offsets stay valid\n\n```python\ndef find_pii(text, page):\n    out = []\n    for kind, rx in PATTERNS.items():\n        for m in rx.finditer(text):\n            v = re.sub(r"\\D", "", m.group())\n            if kind == "AADHAAR" and not verhoeff_ok(v):\n                continue\n            out.append({"type": kind, "page": page,\n                        "start": m.start(), "end": m.end()})\n    return out\n```	claude-sonnet-5-5	21252	481	4702	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-23 11:14:56.284162+00	2026-10-23 11:32:57.173777+00
