910feb78-9ebd-406f-b189-0ff7745f6989	c7135b97-d088-42f6-9108-0f460c34861a	f7516771-4d01-4d7a-9e96-649c87a1c701	484	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Explain PSI and KS tests and their use\n**Both compare live feature distributions to the training baseline; drift triggers retraining.**\n- PSI: bin baseline (e.g., deciles), compare bin proportions live vs. baseline.\n- PSI = Σ (actual% − expected%) × ln(actual% / expected%).\n- PSI <0.1 stable; 0.1–0.25 watch; >0.25 investigate or retrain.\n- KS: max gap between two empirical CDFs; p-value tests significance.\n- KS for continuous features; over-flags on large samples, so pair with effect size.\n- IDP: drift breach → retrain → champion/challenger in SageMaker Model Registry.	claude-opus-5-5	7848	498	2987	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-27 06:01:27.251056+00	2026-10-27 06:01:27.215381+00
