b63c4d4a-eb04-4f1b-8a2c-08c2d386ff5a	37ed911e-34d2-48c8-94d2-9ddced0e1e94	9aafb974-7292-4cd2-8847-b348d20c9c6c	310	assistant	agent	screen_analyzer	\N	**Problem:** The chat list `skills` has repeated items and is cut off in the OCR. I assume the task is to remove duplicates and keep the original order.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\n1. Create an empty "seen" container\n2. For each skill in order:\n3.   If not seen, keep it and mark it seen\n4. Return the kept skills\n```\n\n**Code:**\n```python\nskills = ["Python", "FastAPI", "Python", "LangGraph", "FastAPI"]\n\nunique = list(dict.fromkeys(skills))  # dict keys are unique and keep insertion order\nprint(unique)  # ['Python', 'FastAPI', 'LangGraph']\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- Idea: dict keys are unique and keep insertion order, so duplicates collapse.\n- Why correct: the first occurrence of each skill is inserted, and later ones are ignored.\n- Edge cases: empty list, single item, all duplicates, and case differences ("python" vs "Python") are treated as different. All handled except case, which needs `.lower()`.\n- Complexity: O(n) time and O(n) space, versus O(n²) for a nested `in list` check.\n\n**Alternate method:** `set(skills)` is O(n) time and O(n) space and is shorter, but it loses order. `collections.Counter(skills)` gives each skill's count if the task is to count duplicates.	claude-sonnet-5-5	5046	789	7181	{}	2026-10-27 09:55:18.909255+00	2026-10-27 09:55:18.805923+00
