d6224ba4-8975-4144-8b6b-3e9946f1013a	909ffd7b-adfa-4aed-9284-3434de02d3ce	59522f29-3985-4ebd-8e04-fbc2cebe7f55	2	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Workflow vs agent difference\n**A workflow follows a predefined path that I write in code, while an agent lets the LLM decide its own next step and tool calls at runtime.**\n- In a workflow, the steps, branches and order are fixed, so behaviour is predictable, testable and cheap.\n- An agent runs in a loop: it reasons, picks a tool, observes the result, and repeats until done.\n- The trade-off is that agents handle open-ended tasks but cost more, are slower and need guardrails and observability.\n- In IDP I used n8n workflows for fixed steps, and in APA a supervisor agent on AgentCore routes notices to specialist agents.	claude-opus-5-5	4290	517	2683	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "unknown"}}	2026-10-27 16:34:46.174533+00	2026-10-27 16:34:46.645511+00
