1f8432a5-f982-42d4-b67b-714d07c4c831	909ffd7b-adfa-4aed-9284-3434de02d3ce	54d20b61-8173-4bd0-9fdb-09284900f031	6	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: APA retries and failures when an external API was down\n\n**In APA I used a circuit breaker with retry and resume, plus a fallback chain from API to web automation to OCR-RPA, so a down API never lost work.**\n- When the external API failed repeatedly, the circuit breaker opened, so we stopped hammering it and paused those jobs.\n- Each job saved its progress, so once the API recovered, it resumed from the failed step instead of restarting.\n- If the API stayed unavailable, we fell back to web automation, and then to OCR-RPA as the last option.\n- API responses went through SQS before persistence, so a storage failure never lost a fetched response.	claude-opus-5-5	4630	519	2821	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "unknown"}}	2026-10-27 16:38:28.929285+00	2026-10-27 16:38:28.222626+00
