9bc697bb-2c5c-4c48-8d7f-2c8aca1db7ab	f022a035-22db-48ae-8763-f72c4f0a9129	77e01d5e-3690-44f4-a088-cf2a2c87f995	92	assistant	agent	screen_analyzer	\N	**Problem:** Task 1: `get_total_minutes` must ignore skipped sessions. Task 2: return each user's longest run of consecutive days with a non-skipped session. I assume the method returns `{user_id: streak}`, as `fmt_map` suggests. If it takes a `user_id`, return just that one value.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\n1. Task 1: add the check "if not skipped" before adding minutes\n2. days = dict user -> set of days (non-skipped only)\n3. for each session: create the user's set, add the day if not skipped\n4. for each user, for each day d in the set:\n5.   if d-1 not in the set: count d, d+1, ... while present\n6. best = max run length (0 if no days)\n```\n\n**Code:**\n```python\ndef get_total_minutes(self, user_id: str) -> int:\n    total = 0\n    for s in self.sessions:\n        if s.user_id == user_id and not s.skipped:  # skipped counts as 0\n            total += s.minutes_listened\n    return total\n\ndef get_longest_daily_streak_by_user(self):\n    days = {}\n    for s in self.sessions:\n        if s.user_id not in days:\n            days[s.user_id] = set()\n        if not s.skipped:\n            days[s.user_id].add(s.day)\n    result = {}\n    for user, ds in days.items():\n        best = 0\n        for d in ds:\n            if d - 1 not in ds:  # only start counting at a run's first day\n                length = 1\n                while d + length in ds:\n                    length += 1\n                best = max(best, length)\n        result[user] = best\n    return result\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- Idea: only start counting at a run's first day, so each day is visited about once.\n- Why correct: the set holds only non-skipped days, so duplicates merge and skipped days never count.\n- Edge cases: no sessions, all skipped (0), duplicate days, gaps, unsorted input, negative days; handled.\n- Complexity: O(S) time and space; rescanning the sessions for every day would be O(S·D).\n\n**Alternate method:** Sort each user's distinct days and scan with a running counter, O(S log S) time and O(S) space; simpler but slower than the set approach.	claude-sonnet-5-5	5653	1236	9876	{}	2026-10-28 07:42:47.919848+00	2026-10-28 07:42:49.931646+00
