1f6271f3-f2a6-47d7-8a90-65cb08a7fbbe	f022a035-22db-48ae-8763-f72c4f0a9129	12efa468-b792-49b0-88e4-1520a3276abd	96	assistant	agent	screen_analyzer	\N	**Problem:** Same task, scrolled further. `get_total_minutes` ignores skipped sessions. `get_longest_daily_streak_by_user()` returns `Dict[str, int]` with each user's longest run of consecutive days. Same-day sessions count once, and all-skipped users appear with 0.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\n1. Task 1: sum minutes only for this user's non-skipped sessions\n2. days = dict user -> set of days; create the set for every user\n3. Add the day to the set only if the session is not skipped\n4. For each user, for each day d in the set:\n5.   if d-1 not in the set: count d, d+1, ... while present\n6. result[user] = longest run (0 if the set is empty)\n```\n\n**Code:**\n```python\ndef get_total_minutes(self, user_id: str) -> int:\n    total = 0\n    for s in self.sessions:\n        if s.user_id == user_id and not s.skipped:  # skipped counts as 0\n            total += s.minutes_listened\n    return total\n\ndef get_longest_daily_streak_by_user(self):\n    days = {}\n    for s in self.sessions:\n        if s.user_id not in days:\n            days[s.user_id] = set()      # skipped-only users still appear\n        if not s.skipped:\n            days[s.user_id].add(s.day)   # set dedups same-day sessions\n    result = {}\n    for user, ds in days.items():\n        best = 0\n        for d in ds:\n            if d - 1 not in ds:          # only start at a run's first day\n                length = 1\n                while d + length in ds:\n                    length += 1\n                best = max(best, length)\n        result[user] = best\n    return result\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- Idea: a set dedups days, and counting only from run starts visits each day once.\n- Why correct: every run has exactly one start, a day whose previous day is absent.\n- Edge cases: one day, same-day duplicates, all skipped (0), gaps, 500 days, 0-based days: handled.\n- Complexity: O(S) time, O(S) space; brute force sorting or rescanning per day is O(S²).\n\n**Alternate method:** Sort each user's unique days and scan once, O(S log S) time and O(S) space; simpler to read but slower than the set approach.	claude-sonnet-5-5	5990	1073	8572	{}	2026-10-28 07:43:40.203227+00	2026-10-28 07:43:40.417206+00
