a0d12ba4-f8a3-440a-8a20-73c18228c1c3	f022a035-22db-48ae-8763-f72c4f0a9129	a9028bab-e93b-48cf-be28-6fdfb0cbae85	182	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Which parts are AWS-specific, and does it support multi-cloud?\n**Audit Process Automation is AWS-native and tied to AWS, but my Intelligent Document Processing project is designed to be cloud-agnostic for multi-cloud.**\n- In Audit Process Automation, Lambda, SQS, EventBridge Scheduler and Bedrock AgentCore are AWS-specific, so that system runs only on AWS.\n- In Intelligent Document Processing, storage goes through an abstraction layer, so the same code works with S3, Azure Blob or MinIO.\n- Kafka is the control bus instead of a cloud-specific queue, and the services run in Docker containers, so they can move between clouds.\n- A LiteLLM adapter keeps the LLM layer provider-agnostic, so we can switch away from Bedrock without rewriting the agents.	claude-opus-5-5	7695	829	3248	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-28 08:10:44.880264+00	2026-10-28 08:10:44.881793+00
