5a0f6c0d-6363-4eb4-b214-ef899769baf1	59e01f6e-dfd8-4328-a8fb-2e91d9dae01e	78978c79-2f90-40dc-ad69-adba7e660759	13	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Schema for documents, chunks, embeddings and ingestion status\n**I'd use three PostgreSQL tables: documents, chunks with a pgvector embedding column, and ingestion jobs that track each pipeline stage.**\n- The documents table stores the S3 location, a content hash for deduplication, and a tenant ID for row-level security.\n- Each chunk links to its document, keeps its order and text, and stores the embedding and the embedding model used.\n- Recording the model name lets me re-embed only the affected chunks when we switch embedding models.\n- Ingestion jobs record the stage, status, attempt count and last error, so failed documents can be retried or resumed.\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE Documents (\n    DocumentID INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    TenantID INT,\n    SourceUri VARCHAR(500),\n    ContentHash VARCHAR(64),\n    Status VARCHAR(20),\n    CreatedAt TIMESTAMP\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE Chunks (\n    ChunkID INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    DocumentID INT REFERENCES Documents(DocumentID),\n    ChunkIndex INT,\n    Content TEXT,\n    Embedding VECTOR(768),\n    EmbeddingModel VARCHAR(100)\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE IngestionJobs (\n    JobID INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    DocumentID INT REFERENCES Documents(DocumentID),\n    Stage VARCHAR(30),\n    Status VARCHAR(20),\n    Attempts INT,\n    LastError TEXT,\n    UpdatedAt TIMESTAMP\n);\n```	claude-opus-5-5	5654	1220	4898	{"roles": {"interviewee": "unknown", "interviewer": "mic"}}	2026-10-29 04:42:07.519422+00	2026-10-29 04:42:08.656218+00
