e77eea3b-64c2-42bc-a0d2-bb262f84249b	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	3174870b-0862-4f9c-ba8a-22892bc77b47	79	assistant	agent	screen_analyzer	\N	**Problem:** Interpreting the garbled OCR as: reverse the letters of a string while special characters (`@`, `#`) stay at their original positions. Example: `a@bcd#te` → `e@tdc#ba`.\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\n1. Convert the string to a list; set i = 0, j = n-1\n2. While i < j:\n3.   If s[i] is not a letter: i++\n4.   Else if s[j] is not a letter: j--\n5.   Else swap s[i], s[j]; i++; j--\n6. Join the list and return it\n```\n\n**Code:**\n```python\ndef is_letter(c):\n    return ('a' <= c <= 'z') or ('A' <= c <= 'Z')\n\ndef reverse_keep_special(s):\n    chars = list(s)\n    i, j = 0, len(chars) - 1\n    while i < j:\n        if not is_letter(chars[i]):\n            i += 1\n        elif not is_letter(chars[j]):\n            j -= 1\n        else:\n            chars[i], chars[j] = chars[j], chars[i]\n            i += 1\n            j -= 1\n    result = ""\n    for c in chars:\n        result += c\n    return result\n\ninput_string = "a@bcd#te"\noutput_string = reverse_keep_special(input_string)\nprint(output_string)  # e@tdc#ba\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- Idea: Two pointers swap only letters and skip special characters, so those stay fixed.\n- Why correct: Each swap pairs the outermost unswapped letters; specials are never moved.\n- Edge cases: empty, single character, all specials, no specials, uppercase letters, digits (treated as special), all handled.\n- Complexity: O(n) time, O(n) space; brute force with a stack plus re-insertion is also O(n) but needs more passes.\n\n**Alternate method:** Collect the letters into a list, then rebuild the string by popping from the end at each letter position. This is O(n) time and O(n) space, simpler but uses an extra pass.	claude-sonnet-5-5	3716	1753	14780	{}	2026-10-29 06:35:09.389165+00	2026-10-29 06:35:09.49128+00
