113122a1-6793-45f8-94b4-7db0ffc46d89	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	704ded4e-7ca9-45cd-b739-57fcf621b368	98	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Finish the reverse code using isalpha\n\n**I'll keep my two pointers and use `isalpha()` to skip special characters, so only letters get swapped.**\n\n```python\ninput_string = "a@bcd#e"\nchars_list = list(input_string)\ni, j = 0, len(chars_list) - 1\nwhile i < j:\n    if not chars_list[i].isalpha():\n        i += 1\n    elif not chars_list[j].isalpha():\n        j -= 1\n    else:\n        chars_list[i], chars_list[j] = chars_list[j], chars_list[i]\n        i += 1\n        j -= 1\nprint("".join(chars_list))  # e@dcb#a\n```\n\n- If either pointer is on a non-letter, I move only that pointer, so `@` and `#` keep their positions.\n- When both pointers are on letters, I swap them and move both inward, which takes O(n) time without any built-in reverse.	claude-opus-5-5	8876	789	3064	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 06:38:11.663296+00	2026-10-29 06:38:10.875058+00
