90561cb3-4c13-4eb8-823e-807d162bd727	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	68075465-7843-40bf-86e7-a0b8c7dc8e23	154	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Write a decorator that times a function\n\n**I'll write a `timer` decorator whose wrapper records the time before and after calling the function, then prints the difference.**\n\n```python\nimport time\n\ndef timer(func):\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n        start = time.perf_counter()\n        result = func(*args, **kwargs)\n        print(f"{func.__name__} took {time.perf_counter() - start:.6f} seconds")\n        return result\n    return wrapper\n\n@timer\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n\nprint(add(2, 3))  # add took 0.000001 seconds, then 5\n```\n\n- The wrapper takes `*args, **kwargs` so it can time any function, and it returns the result so the original output is unchanged.\n- I use `time.perf_counter()` because it is a high-resolution clock meant for measuring durations, and the `time` module is needed since timing requires a clock.	claude-opus-5-5	9026	643	2938	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 06:44:29.633615+00	2026-10-29 06:44:29.345674+00
