8fbb2447-3ec2-410d-97a0-c2d2875fc514	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	7db3e3ca-7812-49d3-9e60-9669211a50b4	390	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: REST API design pattern and request flow in FastAPI\n**In FastAPI I follow a layered pattern: routers handle HTTP, Pydantic schemas validate, a service layer holds logic, and a repository talks to the database.**\n- A request reaches an `APIRouter` endpoint, where Pydantic validates the body, path and query parameters automatically.\n- Dependency injection through `Depends` supplies the database session and the authentication check, so endpoints stay thin.\n- The endpoint calls the service layer, which applies business rules and uses a repository to query PostgreSQL.\n- `response_model` shapes the output with proper status codes, and long-running work goes to Celery, which returns a task ID.\n\n```text\n+--------------------------+\n| Client (GET/POST/PUT/DEL)|\n+--------------------------+\n             v\n+--------------------------+\n| APIRouter + Pydantic     |\n+--------------------------+\n             v\n+--------------------------+\n| Depends: DB session/auth |\n+--------------------------+\n             v\n+-----------+  +-----------+\n| Service   |->| Celery    |\n+-----------+  +-----------+\n             v\n+--------------------------+\n| Repository -> PostgreSQL |\n+--------------------------+\n```	claude-opus-5-5	8484	833	3532	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 07:02:31.185846+00	2026-10-29 07:02:32.505233+00
