a8daa88d-0a59-4035-80f4-8899afb343f3	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	4edf99c2-76a4-4a98-845b-d7fb87c1f733	440	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Write an ORM query\n\n**Here is a SQLAlchemy query that fetches active users, sorted by name, without any raw SQL.**\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine, Column, Integer, String, Boolean\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base, Session\nBase = declarative_base()\nclass User(Base):\n    __tablename__ = "users"\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\n    name = Column(String(50))\n    is_active = Column(Boolean)\nengine = create_engine("sqlite://"); Base.metadata.create_all(engine)\nwith Session(engine) as s:\n    s.add_all([User(name="Ravi", is_active=True), User(name="Asha", is_active=True)]); s.commit()\n    print([u.name for u in s.query(User).filter(User.is_active).order_by(User.name).all()])  # ['Asha', 'Ravi']\n```\n\n- The `User` class maps to the `users` table, and `filter` with `order_by` makes SQLAlchemy generate a parameterized `SELECT ... WHERE ... ORDER BY`.\n- In Django the same query is `User.objects.filter(is_active=True).order_by("name")`, which returns a lazy QuerySet.	claude-opus-5-5	8541	1126	4514	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 07:06:15.881211+00	2026-10-29 07:06:15.657787+00
