37c8e08f-5ed4-4573-870c-c791b9882aaa	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	272ab2dc-4d14-4b4c-a72a-3576d425def4	442	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Benefits of using an ORM\n\n**An ORM lets us work with database rows as Python objects, so code is safer, faster to write, and easier to maintain than raw SQL.**\n- It sends values as bound parameters instead of raw string input, which prevents SQL injection by default.\n- The same model code runs on PostgreSQL, MySQL or SQL Server, because the ORM generates the right SQL dialect.\n- Relationships, joins and schema migrations are handled through models, using Alembic with SQLAlchemy or Django migrations.\n- The trade-off is that complex reporting queries or N+1 lookups can be slow, so I use eager loading or raw SQL there.	claude-opus-5-5	8515	468	2616	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 07:06:24.746578+00	2026-10-29 07:06:23.866068+00
