136cf639-380e-4705-8548-cefa13829ebe	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	d3d3ba72-959e-4eee-a708-d4f4b31bf87a	450	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Write an ORM query\n\n**Here is a SQLAlchemy query that fetches the active users sorted by name, with no raw SQL.**\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine, select, String\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import DeclarativeBase, Mapped, mapped_column, Session\n\nclass Base(DeclarativeBase): pass\nclass User(Base):\n    __tablename__ = "users"\n    id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(primary_key=True)\n    name: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(50))\n    is_active: Mapped[bool]\n\nengine = create_engine("sqlite://"); Base.metadata.create_all(engine)\nwith Session(engine) as s:\n    s.add_all([User(name="Bo", is_active=True), User(name="Al", is_active=True), User(name="Cy", is_active=False)]); s.commit()\n    print([u.name for u in s.scalars(select(User).where(User.is_active).order_by(User.name))])  # ['Al', 'Bo']\n```\n\n- `select(User).where(...).order_by(...)` builds the query, and the session runs it with bound parameters.\n- In Django, the same query is `User.objects.filter(is_active=True).order_by("name")`.	claude-opus-5-5	8596	1093	3743	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 07:06:55.314083+00	2026-10-29 07:06:54.584277+00
