c7017653-16b0-495d-9a1a-0fb2d92f56c6	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	f5a31a33-5a41-4a69-9f3b-2d015df96118	463	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: ORM query for third-highest salary (employee + salary tables)\n\n**I rank salaries with DENSE_RANK in a subquery, then join employees and keep rank three.**\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy import select, func\n\nranked = select(\n    Salary.emp_id, Salary.amount,\n    func.dense_rank().over(order_by=Salary.amount.desc()).label("rnk"),\n).subquery()\n\nstmt = (select(Employee.name, ranked.c.amount)\n        .join(ranked, ranked.c.emp_id == Employee.emp_id)\n        .where(ranked.c.rnk == 3))\n\nrows = session.execute(stmt).all()  # 90k,80k,80k,70k -> [("Ravi", 70000)]\n```\n\n- `dense_rank` gives tied salaries the same rank, so two people at 80k don't push out the real third value.\n- If they only need the value, I'd write `select(Salary.amount).distinct().order_by(Salary.amount.desc()).offset(2).limit(1)`.	claude-opus-5-5	8603	920	3786	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 07:07:52.131529+00	2026-10-29 07:07:52.611745+00
