62de85c0-32d2-4ca9-853b-48e225885834	03c687bf-0f6d-47ab-9f40-dcd4caa81525	3c59747a-8f67-4378-820f-9f0c1a62bec4	491	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: How to implement authentication and authorization\n\n**I use JWT for authentication and role-based checks on each request for authorization.**\n\n- At login, the auth service checks the hashed password and issues a short-lived signed JWT containing the user ID, tenant and roles.\n- The client sends that token in the Authorization Bearer header, and middleware verifies its signature and expiry, returning 401 if invalid.\n- Then a permission check maps the user's role to allowed actions, so a valid user without rights gets 403.\n- In the Palm Oil SaaS, I built a custom Go IAM service with multi-tenant RBAC, and Postgres row-level security isolated each tenant.\n\n```text\n+-------------------------+\n| Client: login           |\n+-------------------------+\n            |\n            v\n+-------------------------+\n| Go IAM: issue JWT       |\n+-------------------------+\n            |  Bearer token\n            v\n+-------------------------+\n| Middleware: verify, 401 |\n+-------------------------+\n            |\n            v\n+-------------------------+\n| RBAC check: 403         |\n+-------------------------+\n            |\n            v\n+-------------------------+\n| Postgres RLS            |\n+-------------------------+\n```	claude-opus-5-5	8714	887	4048	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 07:12:53.046929+00	2026-10-29 07:12:52.799992+00
