22fd3a78-d5a1-4789-89b8-621a189a709f	67de7202-5b33-43b0-b70f-06323a6cc71e	860bc1df-7689-4cd9-bf35-dfc87f57fe04	233	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: What do you use for orchestration?\n**I orchestrate at two levels: LangGraph and Bedrock AgentCore for the agents, and n8n with a Kafka control bus for the wider workflow.**\n- In the IDP project, LangGraph runs the generation-critique-revise loop, so a critic checks each draft and sends it back when it falls short.\n- In APA, a supervisor agent on Bedrock AgentCore routes work between the Notice-Summarizing, Reply and Critic agents.\n- n8n orchestrates the business workflow steps, while Kafka carries control events between the sixteen-plus microservices and agents.\n- Celery with RabbitMQ runs the heavy background jobs, which keeps the agents and APIs responsive.	claude-opus-5-5	9540	865	3702	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 10:17:34.304203+00	2026-10-29 10:17:34.307527+00
