9d7478f5-5dbf-4548-bf7d-02c762260116	67de7202-5b33-43b0-b70f-06323a6cc71e	9d5b7df5-6790-4ade-994a-ebb40749fb11	282	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Multi-agent? Workflow crashes mid-run at turn 7: how to recover?\n**It's a multi-agent system, and I'd checkpoint state after every turn so a crash at turn 7 resumes from turn 7.**\n- In APA, a supervisor routes work to the Summarizing, Reply and Critic agents, so the run spans several agents.\n- After each turn, I persist the messages, tool results and current step to PostgreSQL, keyed by run ID.\n- On restart, I reload the last checkpoint instead of replaying six turns, which saves both latency and tokens.\n- Side-effect tools carry an idempotency key checked against the audit log, so resuming never sends a reply twice.\n\n```text\n+--------------------+\n| Supervisor agent   |\n+--------------------+\n          |\n          v\n+--------------------+\n| Agent turn N       |\n+--------------------+\n          |\n          v\n+--------------------+\n| Checkpoint (PG)    |\n+--------------------+\n          | crash\n          v\n+--------------------+\n| Resume at turn N   |\n+--------------------+\n```	claude-opus-5-5	9564	1173	5098	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 10:21:08.546898+00	2026-10-29 10:21:08.55028+00
