b2d561ca-a751-49bd-8388-4693701774b5	67de7202-5b33-43b0-b70f-06323a6cc71e	9dee0688-b15b-449f-a59d-5dd1514af6f4	417	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Difference between full-text (tsvector) search and vector search, likely\n\n**Full-text search matches the actual words in a query, while vector search with pgvector matches the meaning through embeddings.**\n- Postgres full-text search turns text into a `tsvector` of stemmed words, uses a GIN index, and ranks results with `ts_rank`.\n- pgvector stores embeddings and ranks by cosine distance, using an HNSW or IVFFlat approximate index for speed.\n- Full-text is exact on IDs, codes and names but misses synonyms, while vector search catches paraphrases but can miss exact terms.\n- That is why hybrid search runs both and merges the two rankings, often with reciprocal rank fusion.	claude-opus-5-5	9452	1001	4398	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-29 10:30:48.454069+00	2026-10-29 10:30:48.457489+00
