139d0af3-726b-4ca9-b5cc-91b531699680	f5ee4145-4dcd-46f3-989d-bb7059873e8a	bc6f7546-e6ee-4192-bffe-0868eaf0c620	359	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Hands-on classical ML (random forest, decision tree, XGBoost)?\n**My experience with classical ML is on the MLOps side: I built and ran the pipelines around these models, but I did not design or tune the models myself.**\n- In IDP, the anomaly-detection and classification pipelines ran scikit-learn, XGBoost, LightGBM, random forest and Isolation Forest.\n- I set up SageMaker training and tuning jobs, with MLflow tracking every run, so we could compare algorithms in bake-off runs.\n- The best model was promoted through SageMaker Model Registry using champion/challenger, so a new model replaced production only if it performed better.\n- I also added drift detection with PSI and KS tests, which automatically triggered retraining when the input data shifted.	claude-opus-5-5	9876	626	3056	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-30 12:25:40.164513+00	2026-10-30 12:25:40.292865+00
