b3546e0a-86e7-49bf-b844-8ff3c419d5e6	10180534-37c3-45d8-8232-25e45cd848ee	94613aa7-aed7-48c4-9a9e-ad866656df20	94	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Explain your RAG architecture and why RAG is needed\n**We need RAG because the LLM doesn't know our private, changing documents, so we retrieve relevant chunks at query time and ground its answer in them.**\n- Fine-tuning is costly and goes stale, while RAG stays current once new documents are indexed and it reduces hallucination.\n- In IDP, I chunk the extracted documents, embed them with SentenceTransformer, and store the vectors in pgvector.\n- At query time, LangChain retrieves the closest chunks and adds graph entity context before prompting the LLM.\n- I measure retrieval quality and answer faithfulness with RAGAS, so chunking or prompt changes are validated with metrics.\n\n```text\n+-----------------------+\n| Extracted documents   |\n+-----------------------+\n     | chunk + embed\n     v\n+-----------------------+\n| SentenceTransformer   |\n+-----------------------+\n     v\n+----------+   +-------------+\n| pgvector |-->| LangChain + |\n|          |   | graph ctx   |\n+----------+   +-------------+\n     v\n+-----------------------+\n| LLM answer -> RAGAS   |\n+-----------------------+\n```	claude-opus-5-5	8243	949	4225	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 08:34:44.027077+00	2026-10-31 08:34:44.037947+00
