35c2edf3-afb6-4e40-92c7-4c6fbbdb61cb	10180534-37c3-45d8-8232-25e45cd848ee	4f308259-81cb-4311-bfee-8243fd6cca0b	250	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: What is actually different between MCP and an API?\n\n**The route logic looks similar, but MCP uses one standard protocol for discovery and calls, while a REST API is a fixed endpoint contract that client code must already know.**\n- With REST, each endpoint has its own URL, verbs and payloads, so the agent developer hard-codes how to call it.\n- MCP uses JSON-RPC messages, so every server exposes the same `tools/list` and `tools/call` methods.\n- The agent first calls `tools/list` and receives each tool's name, description and JSON input schema, which the LLM reads directly.\n- MCP also opens a session with an initialize handshake, so client and server agree on supported features before any tool call.\n- As a result, I can plug a new tool into any agent without writing new client code, while the REST services underneath stay unchanged.	claude-opus-5-5	9210	659	3359	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 08:43:18.427085+00	2026-10-31 08:43:18.430498+00
