40c94c76-37ed-43b7-ad8d-488e32a068b2	10180534-37c3-45d8-8232-25e45cd848ee	6165b0b0-589a-4e39-95eb-3763ef421a7c	353	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Design principle vs design pattern\n**A design principle is a general guideline for writing good code, while a design pattern is a proven, reusable solution to a specific recurring design problem.**\n- Principles like SOLID, DRY and KISS tell you what good design looks like, but not how to implement it.\n- Patterns like Singleton, Factory, Observer, Strategy and Decorator give a concrete structure you can apply directly.\n- So patterns usually put principles into practice; for example, Strategy follows the open-closed principle by adding behaviour without editing existing code.\n- In my work, I used the adapter pattern with LiteLLM, which keeps our code independent of any single LLM provider.	claude-opus-5-5	9344	247	1904	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 08:49:51.991441+00	2026-10-31 08:49:51.994901+00
