4a02f717-6cc7-4c91-ba56-9cf204dd551d	66280805-b450-4556-9a00-cca2fea025d2	dfb0ea6a-3433-431f-90ee-077e3f945be4	89	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: APA architecture and end-to-end flow\n\n**The platform polls each taxpayer's notices on a schedule, persists them through SQS, and lets AgentCore agents draft replies with action plans for human review.**\n\n- EventBridge Scheduler triggers Lambda fetchers per tenant, which try the API first, then web automation, then the OCR-RPA fallback.\n- A circuit breaker retries and resumes failed fetches, and responses go through SQS so persistence stays decoupled from slow external sources.\n- On AgentCore, a supervisor routes each notice to the Notice-Summarizing agent, then the Reply agent, and the Critic agent reviews the draft.\n- Approved drafts and action plans reach users through Firebase push, while CloudWatch-based AgentCore Observability traces every agent step.\n\n```text\n+------------------------+\n| EventBridge Scheduler  |\n+------------------------+\n       |\n       v\n+------------------------+\n| Lambda fetch (API/RPA) |\n+------------------------+\n       v\n+-------+    +-----------+\n|  SQS  |--> | Persist   |\n+-------+    +-----------+\n       v\n| AgentCore supervisor   |\n| Summarize>Reply>Critic |\n       v\n| Firebase push -> user  |\n```	claude-opus-5-5	7942	808	3829	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 09:36:52.953482+00	2026-10-31 09:36:52.96022+00
