56390c06-404e-4207-9638-e690bb7c8d72	66280805-b450-4556-9a00-cca2fea025d2	64551706-809e-4c0d-8b3c-972b87969dd5	110	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Where the persistence Lambda stores the data\n\n**The persistence Lambda consumes from SQS and writes into [PostgreSQL / Aurora], with raw documents in S3 and job state cached in Redis.**\n\n- The fetcher Lambdas only push responses onto SQS, so the persistence Lambda is the one component that writes to the database.\n- Structured notice data and reply drafts go into [PostgreSQL / Aurora], and each row is scoped per tenant for isolation.\n- Raw notice files and OCR inputs go to S3, while Redis holds job status and KPI counters for fast lookups.\n- Because SQS sits in between, a database slowdown only grows the queue, and failed messages are retried instead of lost.\n\n```text\n+------------------------+\n| Lambda fetchers        |\n+------------------------+\n       |\n       v\n+------------------------+\n| SQS queue              |\n+------------------------+\n       |\n       v\n+------------------------+\n| Persistence Lambda     |\n+------------------------+\n       v\n+------------+  +--------+\n| [Postgres] |  |   S3   |\n+------------+  +--------+\n```	claude-opus-5-5	9429	697	3605	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 09:39:57.232804+00	2026-10-31 09:39:57.238553+00
