3e1f1379-5765-41b3-9e6a-572792934a4d	66280805-b450-4556-9a00-cca2fea025d2	047ad04e-901f-497d-a2e5-87283dc03abd	170	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Handling shared state when agents run in parallel for one query\n\n**In LangGraph, parallel agents run in the same step, and reducers merge their state updates so no agent overwrites another's result.**\n\n- A fan-out edge, or the Send API, starts each agent as a parallel branch on the same input state.\n- Each agent writes to its own key, or to a list key with an append reducer, so concurrent writes merge cleanly.\n- Without a reducer, two branches writing the same key in one step raise an error instead of silently overwriting each other.\n- An aggregator node then combines the merged results into one answer.\n- The checkpointer saves after each step, so if one branch fails, only that branch reruns on resume.\n\n```text\n+----------------+\n|  Query / State |\n+----------------+\n   |          |\n   v          v\n+-------+  +-------+\n|Agent A|  |Agent B|\n+-------+  +-------+\n   |          |\n   v          v\n+----------------+\n| Reducer merge  |\n+----------------+\n        |\n        v\n+----------------+\n|  Aggregator    |\n+----------------+\n```	claude-opus-5-5	9312	805	4075	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 09:45:10.459806+00	2026-10-31 09:45:10.464443+00
