98b86c68-df30-45f5-ad5b-75f5dfae8807	66280805-b450-4556-9a00-cca2fea025d2	68dbd3fc-7fd4-4d96-8009-fbfc3b72d950	208	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: Checkpointing design for a banking multi-agent system\n\n**For a banking system, I'd use a durable Postgres checkpointer on Aurora instead of in-memory, so state survives crashes and every step is auditable.**\n\n- LangGraph's Postgres checkpointer saves state after every step under a thread ID, so any instance can resume the flow.\n- Each thread ID maps to one customer request, and row-level security keeps each tenant's checkpoints isolated.\n- Checkpoints are encrypted at rest, IAM limits which services can read them, and an append-only audit log records every agent action.\n- An interrupt pauses before anything reaches the customer, so a reviewer approves sensitive replies and failures show a pending status, never a partial answer.\n\n```text\n+------------------+\n| Customer request |\n+------------------+\n         |\n         v\n+------------------+   +-------------+\n| LangGraph agents |-->| Aurora PG   |\n| (parallel)       |   | checkpoints |\n+------------------+   +-------------+\n         v\n+------------------+   +-------------+\n| Aggregator+review|-->| Audit log   |\n+------------------+   +-------------+\n```	claude-opus-5-5	9152	1165	4968	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 09:47:41.284732+00	2026-10-31 09:47:41.287705+00
