75ae76bd-2ed3-4c18-a6f5-8a95f55605b8	66280805-b450-4556-9a00-cca2fea025d2	bfa44422-806b-4424-a3c7-424ba46fef15	219	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: How checkpointing restarts a workflow after an agent fails\n\n**Checkpointing lets me resume the workflow from the last saved step, so a failed agent never forces the whole workflow to restart.**\n\n- LangGraph saves a checkpoint after every step under the thread ID, holding the full shared state.\n- If one agent fails mid-step, the successful agents' outputs are kept as pending writes on that checkpoint.\n- I resume by invoking the graph again with the same thread ID and no new input, so only the failed agent reruns.\n- Because the checkpointer is durable in Postgres, even a crashed process resumes on another instance, and I can replay from any earlier checkpoint ID.	claude-opus-5-5	9011	624	2910	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 09:48:25.24268+00	2026-10-31 09:48:25.245637+00
