9a8f966d-8884-49d7-b64d-dbab418330ac	66280805-b450-4556-9a00-cca2fea025d2	3bd9e914-d149-413e-8ff8-f518fa6b5832	349	assistant	agent	conversor	\N	Q: How to evaluate the RAG pipeline before production, and which metrics\n\n**I evaluate it with RAGAS against a golden test set, and release only when retrieval and answer metrics pass agreed thresholds.**\n\n- First, I build a golden set of real questions with expected answers and source chunks, including tables and appendix questions.\n- For retrieval, I track context precision and context recall, which show whether the right chunks come back and rank high.\n- For generation, I track faithfulness and answer relevancy, so answers stay grounded in the retrieved context instead of hallucinating.\n- I run this in GitLab CI as a release gate and trace runs in Langfuse, so regressions are caught before production.\n\n```text\n+------------------------+\n| Golden Q&A set         |\n+------------------------+\n     |\n     v\n+------------------------+\n| RAG pipeline (dev)     |\n+------------------------+\n     |\n     v\n+------------------------+\n| RAGAS + Langfuse       |\n+------------------------+\n     |\n     v\n+------------------------+\n| GitLab CI gate -> prod |\n+------------------------+\n```	claude-opus-5-5	9753	671	3264	{"roles": {"interviewee": "mic", "interviewer": "loopback"}}	2026-10-31 09:56:02.388887+00	2026-10-31 09:56:02.393753+00
