cade4876-93f9-4dda-8ac4-075343877cf3	66280805-b450-4556-9a00-cca2fea025d2	be39a44e-8167-4255-86a0-9c19ca74f80b	523	assistant	agent	chat	\N	**Corrected answer: I pick models on Bedrock, and the model ID is a per-agent config value.** LiteLLM was only in IDP. In APA the agents run on Bedrock AgentCore.\n\n- **Selection:** I run the same prompts and golden set through each whitelisted Bedrock model, then compare quality, latency and cost.\n- **Per-step choice:** Claude Haiku handles routing, tool selection and classification, where speed and low cost matter. A larger Claude model handles the Reply and Critic agents, which need multi-step reasoning over the chunks and legal nuance.\n- **Changing models:** Each agent reads its Bedrock model ID from config, so moving a step up or down needs no code change.\n- **Fallback:** I choose a second whitelisted model for each step, validated on the same golden set so it is a tested option. If the primary fails or is throttled, the circuit-breaker retry retries and then switches to the fallback.\n- **If the fallback also fails:** The job is saved and resumed later instead of being dropped. The circuit-breaker retry/resume pattern handles this.\n- **Monitoring:** AgentCore Observability in CloudWatch shows which model served each call, along with errors and latency.	claude-sonnet-5-5	5735	814	7208	{}	2026-10-31 10:06:50.201929+00	2026-10-31 10:06:50.207222+00
